   "subject": "Infinite Looping When Rendering in Browser",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">So I added the Hmisc library to my project and added lots of features to one of my applications. I tested everything using R Studio Window and it ran perfectly. However, if I try to launch the new program on chrome it silently goes into an infinite loop. The same issue is also happening in IE and FF.  I have attempted using showReactLog(), uninstalling my libraries and reinstalling, etc. Is this a common issue? What are some common causes of this ? Also, is there any better way to debug than showReactLog()? I am finding it detrimental to debugging because the net of reactions is SO large. <div><br></div><div>I checked my chrome dev tools for any clues and it doesn&#39;t return anything helpful. The returned value is :</div><div>jquery.min.js:4 Synchronous XMLHttpRequest on the main thread is deprecated because of its detrimental effects to the end user&#39;s experience. For more help, check <a href=\"http://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792397313158000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1flbmrzzOTXEhTolRKoIyT\">http://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/</a>. <br></div><div><br></div><div>Any thoughts or explanations would be helpful. I am not understanding why it isn&#39;t breaking with the R window versus the common browsers.</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
