lor:#080\">&quot;id&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;textLegend&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;message&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:{</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;value&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">}},{</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;id&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;legPos&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;message&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:{</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;value&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;right&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">}}]}</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div></code></div><div><br></div>But the trace isn&#39;t actually performing any recursions. There isn&#39;t even a large amount of text being dumped to the console. Maybe it isn&#39;t a true recursion? However, if I debug my program so that it is paused at renderPlot()  I keep hitting the same breakpoint over and over again. Maybe it is a bad call stack?<div><div><br></div><div>The issue does not persist if I change runApp options to &#39;external&#39;. This opens the window in chrome automatically. However, the issue is occurring if the runApp option is set to &#39;Run in Window&#39;. When the R Studio window opens and I choose the &quot;Open in Browser&quot; option the issues begin to occur once more. I will be testing my program on a different computer this afternoon to see if it is the code itself or the studio.  <div><br></div><div>As for software I have the latest Chrome, R 3.2.1, Shiny 0.12.1. </div></div></div></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for your help!</div><div><br></div><div>Amber</div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
